## 3. fxmanifest Validation — Executable Dependency Graph

### dce-core (rebuilt)
```
shared_scripts            (server VM + client VMs)
  └ config.lua            (pure data — no behavior)

server_scripts            (server VM only; order IS the graph)
  runtime/state.lua       ─┐
  runtime/logger.lua      ─┤ constructors register on
  runtime/registry.lua    ─┤ DCE_INTERNAL (server-only)
  runtime/eventbus.lua    ─┤
  runtime/scheduler.lua   ─┤
  runtime/plugin-manager.lua ─┤
  runtime/config-manager.lua ─┤
  runtime/sdk.lua         ─┘
  runtime/bootstrap.lua   ← SINGLE COMPOSITION ROOT
  init.lua                ← exports (static functions)

client_scripts            (client VM only; minimal facade)
  runtime/state.lua       ─┐ pure leaf modules
  runtime/logger.lua      ─┤
  runtime/registry.lua    ─┤
  runtime/eventbus.lua    ─┘
  client/bootstrap.lua    ← client composition root
  client/init.lua         ← client exports
```

- **No module depends on later modules** (constructors before composition root before exports).
- **No circular dependency** (single-directed graph).
- **No duplicate loading** (each file listed exactly once per runtime).
- **No hidden ordering dependency** — the manifest IS the graph; `require()` is gone.

### Dependent resources (validated, unchanged)
All dependents declare `dependency {'dce-core'}` (dce-ai additionally `dce-world`). Per FiveM, this guarantees dce-core fully starts before any dependent script executes — the exports exist before any consumer runs.

| Resource | Declares dependency on | SDK acquisition |
|---|---|---|
| dce-world | dce-core | direct, unconditional |
| dce-ai | dce-core, dce-world | direct, unconditional |
| dce-events | dce-core | direct, unconditional |
| dce-dispatch | dce-core | direct, unconditional |
| dce-evidence | dce-core | direct, unconditional |
| dce-test-suite | dce-core | direct, unconditional |
| dce-controlcenter | dce-core | deterministic single-pass ConnectToCore |

