## 4. Export Validation

All exports are defined as **static functions** in the final server_script (`init.lua`) and final client_script (`client/init.lua`):

| Export | Registered by | Availability |
|---|---|---|
| `GetDCEAPI` | dce-core server/client `init.lua` (static fn) | from first moment the resource is considered "started" — guaranteed before any dependency consumer executes |
| `IsReady` | dce-core server/client `init.lua` (static fn) | same |
| `DCE_Subscribe` | dce-core server/client `init.lua` (static fn) | same |

- Exports are never created lazily, never inside lifecycle callbacks, never removed during operation.
- They **cannot disappear** after reload: every `onResourceStop`/restart re-executes the same static function definitions.
- Consumers cannot receive `No such export` on a cold boot **provided** they declare `dependency {'dce-core'}` — which all DCE resources now do. Any consumer that fails to declare the dependency will now fail-fast with an explicit error (rather than silently degrading).

