## 5. Bootstrap Determinism (Phase 7 Proof)

Every bootstrap phase:

| Requirement | Evidence |
|---|---|
| Executes exactly once | Single composition root invoked once by `init.lua`; constructors execute once per manifest listing |
| No `Wait()` | `grep` of all runtime bootstrap paths shows zero `Wait()` in startup logic (only the Scheduler's normal recurring-tick loop uses `Citizen.Wait`, which is runtime behavior, not startup synchronization) |
| No polling | All 5 `while ... Wait(100)` polling loops removed |
| No retries | Dependent acquisition is a single direct call; fail-fast `error()` on nil |
| No `Citizen.CreateThread` timing dependence | Startup is synchronous single-threaded script execution |
| No frame-order dependence | None — startup is pure script execution order |
| No resource-load race conditions | Eliminated by the `dependency` directive (documented load-before) |

